**Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then \"I\" key\n306-- **Expected**: The characters \"gi\" are typed into the input. No navigation occurs.\n307-\n308:#### Test: G chord times out if second key is delayed\n309-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n310-- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, waits 2 seconds, then presses \"I\" key\n311:- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The chord is cancelled after a short timeout (~1 second).\n312-\n313:#### Test: G followed by unrecognized key does nothing\n314-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n315-- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"X\" key\n316-- **Expected**: Nothing happens. No navigation or modal opens. The app does not error.\n317-\n318:#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts work from different pages\n319-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/settings`\n320-- **Action**: User presses \"C\" key\n321-- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens, same as from any other page.\n322-\n323:#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts do not fire when modal is open\n324:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create issue modal is open\n325-- **Action**: User presses \"G\" then \"I\"\n326-- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The modal remains open. The keystrokes do not trigger navigation shortcuts.\n327-\n328-## My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n329-\n330-**Components**: MyIssuesList, IssueRow, FiltersToolbar\n331-\n332-### MyIssuesList\n333-\n334-#### Test: My Issues page renders with issues grouped by status\n335-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues assigned in statuses: Backlog (2 issues), In Progress (1 issue), Done (1 issue)\n336-- **Expected**: The page displays issues grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n337-\n338-#### Test: My Issues page shows empty state when no issues assigned\n339-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no issues assigned to them\n340-- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No issues assigned to you yet\") instead of an empty list.\n341-\n342-#### Test: Status group is collapsible\n343-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in \"In Progress\" status, the group is expanded\n344-- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n--\n1043-#### Test: Newly created sub-issue appears in the list\n1044:- **Initial state**: User clicked \"Add sub-issue\", the create issue modal is open with parent set to \"ENG-10\"\n1045-- **Action**: User fills in title \"Write unit tests\", sets status to \"Todo\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1046-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new sub-issue (e.g., \"ENG-13 Write unit tests\") appears in the sub-issues list with a gray circle (Todo) status icon. The sub-issue is persisted with its parent reference.\n1047-\n1048-#### Test: Sub-issue status icon updates when status changes\n1049-- **Initial state**: Sub-issue \"ENG-12\" has status \"In Progress\" (yellow half-circle) and is displayed in the parent's sub-issues list\n1050-- **Action**: User navigates to \"ENG-12\", changes its status to \"Done\", and navigates back to the parent issue\n1051-- **Expected**: The sub-issue \"ENG-12\" now shows a green check-circle (Done) icon in the parent's sub-issues list.\n1052-\n1053-#### Test: Multiple sub-issues display in correct order\n1054-- **Initial state**: Parent issue has 4 sub-issues created in order: ENG-11, ENG-12, ENG-13, ENG-14\n1055-- **Expected**: All 4 sub-issues are displayed in the list in a consistent order (e.g., by creation date or identifier).\n1056-\n1057-### ActivityComments\n1058-\n1059-#### Test: Activity/Comments section renders with tab toggle\n1060-- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page, scrolled to the bottom of the left panel\n1061-- **Expected**: The Activity/Comments section is visible with two tab buttons: \"Activity\" and \"Comments\". One tab is active (visually highlighted). A comment input box with a \"Comment\" button is visible at the bottom.\n1062-\n1063-#### Test: Activity tab shows chronological history\n1064-- **Initial state**: An issue has had its status changed from \"Backlog\" to \"Todo\", then assignee changed from unassigned to \"Alice\", then priority changed from \"No Priority\" to \"High\"\n--\n1248-#### Test: Team selector allows changing team\n1249:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" pre-selected. Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist.\n1250-- **Action**: User clicks the Team selector dropdown and selects \"Design\"\n1251-- **Expected**: Team selector now shows \"Design\". The Cycle dropdown updates to show \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" team's cycles.\n1252-\n1253-#### Test: Title field is required\n1254:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1255-- **Action**: User leaves the Title field empty and attempts to submit\n1256-- **Expected**: A validation error appears indicating that title is required. The issue is not created.\n1257-\n1258-#### Test: Title field accepts text input\n1259:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1260-- **Action**: User types \"Implement user authentication\" in the Title field\n1261-- **Expected**: The Title field displays \"Implement user authentication\".\n1262-\n1263-#### Test: Description field supports markdown text entry\n1264:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1265-- **Action**: User types \"## Overview\\nThis issue covers the auth flow\" in the Description text area\n1266-- **Expected**: The Description field accepts and displays the markdown text.\n1267-\n1268-#### Test: Status dropdown defaults to Backlog\n1269:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1270-- **Expected**: The Status dropdown shows \"Backlog\" with a dotted circle icon in gray as the default selected value.\n1271-\n1272-#### Test: Status dropdown shows all status options with icons\n1273:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1274-- **Action**: User clicks the Status dropdown\n1275-- **Expected**: Dropdown shows all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red).\n1276-\n1277-#### Test: Status dropdown allows selecting a different status\n1278:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Status shows \"Backlog\"\n1279-- **Action**: User clicks Status dropdown and selects \"Todo\"\n1280-- **Expected**: Status dropdown now shows \"Todo\" with circle icon in gray.\n1281-\n1282-#### Test: Priority dropdown defaults to No Priority\n1283:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1284-- **Expected**: The Priority dropdown shows \"No Priority\" with dots-horizontal icon in gray as the default value.\n1285-\n1286-#### Test: Priority dropdown shows all priority options with icons\n1287:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1288-- **Action**: User clicks the Priority dropdown\n1289-- **Expected**: Dropdown shows: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray).\n1290-\n1291-#### Test: Priority dropdown allows selecting a priority\n1292:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Priority shows \"No Priority\"\n1293-- **Action**: User clicks Priority dropdown and selects \"High\"\n1294-- **Expected**: Priority dropdown now shows \"High\" with arrow-up icon in orange.\n1295-\n1296-#### Test: Assignee selector is searchable\n1297:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\", \"Carol Lee\".\n1298-- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector and types \"Ali\"\n1299-- **Expected**: The selector filters to show only \"Alice Smith\" with her avatar.\n1300-\n1301-#### Test: Assignee selector allows selecting a member\n1302:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Assignee field is empty\n1303-- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector, types \"Bob\", and clicks \"Bob Jones\"\n1304-- **Expected**: Assignee field shows \"Bob Jones\" with his avatar.\n1305-\n1306-#### Test: Labels multi-select allows selecting multiple labels\n1307:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Labels \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\" exist.\n1308-- **Action**: User clicks Labels selector, selects \"Bug\", then selects \"Feature\"\n1309-- **Expected**: Both \"Bug\" and \"Feature\" appear as colored badges in the Labels field.\n1310-\n1311-#### Test: Labels multi-select allows removing a selected label\n1312:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with \"Bug\" and \"Feature\" labels selected\n1313-- **Action**: User clicks the remove button on the \"Bug\" label badge\n1314-- **Expected**: Only \"Feature\" remains selected in the Labels field.\n1315-\n1316-#### Test: Project selector is searchable\n1317:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Projects \"API Redesign\", \"Mobile App\", \"Dashboard\" exist.\n1318-- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and types \"API\"\n1319-- **Expected**: The selector filters to show only \"API Redesign\".\n1320-\n1321-#### Test: Project selector allows selecting a project\n1322:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Project field is empty\n1323-- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and selects \"Mobile App\"\n1324-- **Expected**: Project field shows \"Mobile App\".\n1325-\n1326-#### Test: Cycle dropdown shows team's available cycles\n1327:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected. Team has cycles \"Sprint 10\" (active) and \"Sprint 11\" (upcoming).\n1328-- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle dropdown\n1329-- **Expected**: Dropdown shows \"Sprint 10\" and \"Sprint 11\". The active cycle is indicated.\n1330-\n1331-#### Test: Cycle dropdown allows selecting a cycle\n1332:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Cycle field is empty\n1333-- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle dropdown and selects \"Sprint 10\"\n1334-- **Expected**: Cycle field shows \"Sprint 10\".\n1335-\n1336-#### Test: Cycle dropdown updates when team is changed\n1337:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected showing its cycles\n1338-- **Action**: User changes team to \"Design\" via the Team selector\n1339-- **Expected**: The Cycle dropdown clears its selection and now shows \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" cycles.\n1340-\n1341-#### Test: Due date picker allows selecting a date\n1342:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Due date field is empty\n1343-- **Action**: User clicks the Due date picker and selects a date (e.g., March 25, 2026)\n1344-- **Expected**: Due date field shows \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n1345-\n1346-#### Test: Due date picker allows clearing the date\n1347:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with due date \"Mar 25, 2026\" set\n1348-- **Action**: User clicks the clear button on the Due date field\n1349-- **Expected**: Due date field is empty again.\n1350-\n1351-#### Test: Parent issue selector is searchable\n1352:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issues \"ENG-1: Setup project\", \"ENG-2: Design database\" exist.\n1353-- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and types \"Setup\"\n1354-- **Expected**: The selector filters to show \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n1355-\n1356-#### Test: Parent issue selector allows selecting a parent\n1357:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Parent issue field is empty\n1358-- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\"\n1359-- **Expected**: Parent issue field shows \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n1360-\n1361-#### Test: Assignee selector can be used multiple times\n1362:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with \"Alice Smith\" selected as assignee\n1363-- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector, clears the selection, types \"Bob\", selects \"Bob Jones\", then repeats to select \"Carol Lee\"\n1364-- **Expected**: Assignee field shows \"Carol Lee\" after the final selection. Each selection correctly replaces the previous one.\n1365-\n1366-#### Test: Labels selector can be used multiple times in sequence\n1367:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with no labels selected\n1368-- **Action**: User selects \"Bug\" label, then opens the selector again and adds \"Feature\", then opens again and removes \"Bug\" and adds \"Improvement\"\n1369-- **Expected**: Labels field shows \"Feature\" and \"Improvement\" as colored badges.\n1370-\n1371-#### Test: Status dropdown can be changed multiple times\n1372:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with Status \"Backlog\"\n1373-- **Action**: User changes status to \"Todo\", then changes it to \"In Progress\", then back to \"Backlog\"\n1374-- **Expected**: Status shows \"Backlog\" after the final change. Each intermediate state was correctly displayed.\n1375-\n1376-### CreateIssueActions\n1377-\n1378-#### Test: Create Issue button is visible and styled\n1379:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1380-- **Expected**: A \"Create Issue\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal with primary styling (accent color background).\n1381-\n1382-#### Test: Cancel button is visible\n1383:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1384-- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal alongside the \"Create Issue\" button.\n1385-\n1386-#### Test: Cancel button closes the modal\n1387:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1388-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n1389-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No issue is created. The user returns to the previous page view.\n1390-\n1391-#### Test: Cancel button discards form data\n1392:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has entered title \"Draft issue\" and selected priority \"High\".\n1393-- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\", then opens the create issue modal again\n1394-- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields reset to defaults (empty title, Backlog status, No Priority). The previously entered data is not retained.\n1395-\n1396-#### Test: Create Issue button submits the form with all fields\n1397:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has filled in: Title \"Implement OAuth\", Description \"Add OAuth support\", Status \"Todo\", Priority \"High\", Assignee \"Alice Smith\", Labels \"Feature\", Project \"API Redesign\", Cycle \"Sprint 10\", Due date \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n1398-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1399-- **Expected**: The issue is created with all specified field values. A brief confirmation showing the new issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-43\") is displayed. The modal closes and the user is navigated to the issues list.\n1400-\n1401-#### Test: Create Issue with only required fields\n1402:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected\n1403-- **Action**: User enters title \"Quick bug fix\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1404-- **Expected**: The issue is created with title \"Quick bug fix\", status \"Backlog\", priority \"No Priority\", and no assignee/labels/project/cycle/due date. The new issue identifier is briefly shown. The modal closes.\n1405-\n1406-#### Test: Created issue appears in the team issues list\n1407-- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for \"Engineering\". The page shows existing issues.\n1408-- **Action**: User clicks \"New Issue\", enters title \"New feature request\", sets status to \"Todo\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1409-- **Expected**: After modal closes, the Team Issues list updates to include \"New feature request\" under the \"Todo\" status group with the correct issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-44\").\n1410-\n1411-#### Test: Created issue with parent appears as sub-issue\n1412:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issue \"ENG-1: Setup project\" exists.\n1413-- **Action**: User enters title \"Write unit tests\", selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\" as parent issue, and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1414-- **Expected**: The issue is created. When navigating to \"ENG-1: Setup project\" detail page, \"Write unit tests\" appears in the sub-issues section.\n1415-\n1416-#### Test: Created issue generates activity history entry\n1417:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1418-- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Track history\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1419-- **Expected**: When viewing the new issue's detail page, the Activity tab shows an initial \"created this issue\" entry with the current user's name and timestamp.\n1420-\n1421-#### Test: Created issue generates inbox notification for assignee\n1422:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Current user is \"Alice Smith\".\n1423-- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Review PR\", assigns it to \"Bob Jones\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1424-- **Expected**: When Bob Jones checks their inbox, a notification appears: \"Alice Smith assigned you to [issue identifier]: Review PR\" with the correct timestamp. The inbox badge count increases.\n1425-\n1426-#### Test: Create Issue button is disabled during submission\n1427:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with valid data entered\n1428-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Issue\"\n1429-- **Expected**: The \"Create Issue\" button becomes disabled (to prevent duplicate submissions) while the request is processing. It re-enables after the operation completes (success or failure).\n1430-\n1431-#### Test: Clicking outside the modal closes it\n1432:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1433-- **Action**: User clicks on the overlay area outside the modal\n1434-- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating an issue.\n1435-\n1436-#### Test: Pressing Escape closes the modal\n1437:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n1438-- **Action**: User presses the Escape key\n1439-- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating an issue.\n1440-\n1441-#### Test: Creating multiple issues in sequence works correctly\n1442-- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for \"Engineering\"\n1443-- **Action**: User creates issue \"First task\" via the modal, then opens the modal again and creates \"Second task\"\n1444-- **Expected**: Both issues appear in the team issues list with sequential identifiers (e.g., \"ENG-43\", \"ENG-44\"). The modal resets correctly between creations.\n1445-\n1446-## Active Cycle Page (`/team:teamId/cycles`)\n1447-\n1448-**Components**: CycleList, CycleDetail, CreateCycle, BurndownChart\n1449-\n1450-### CycleList\n1451-\n1452-#### Test: Cycle list renders all team cycles with name, date range, progress bar, and issue count\n1453-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/eng-1/cycles`. The \"Engineering\" team has 3 cycles: \"Sprint 1\" (Jan 1–Jan 14, 8/10 issues done), \"Sprint 2\" (Jan 15–Jan 28, 3/8 issues done, active), \"Sprint 3\" (Jan 29–Feb 11, 0/5 issues done).\n1454-- **Expected**: A list of 3 cycle rows is displayed. Each row shows the cycle name, date range (e.g., \"Jan 1 – Jan 14\"), a progress bar reflecting the completion percentage (e.g., 80% for Sprint 1), and the issue count (e.g., \"10 issues\"). Rows are ordered chronologically.\n1455-\n1456-#### Test: Active cycle is visually highlighted in the list\n1457-- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles`. \"Sprint 2\" is the active cycle.\n--\n1546-#### Test: Successfully creating a cycle with all fields filled\n1547:- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open. Team has no active cycle.\n1548-- **Action**: User enters \"Sprint 5\" in the Name field, selects Feb 12 as Start date, selects Feb 25 as End date, and clicks \"Create\".\n1549-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The cycle list now includes \"Sprint 5\" with the date range \"Feb 12 – Feb 25\", 0 issues, and an empty progress bar. The new cycle appears in the list.\n1550-\n1551-#### Test: Create cycle validates that name is required\n1552:- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open.\n1553-- **Action**: User leaves the Name field empty, sets start and end dates, and clicks \"Create\".\n1554-- **Expected**: A validation error message appears near the Name field (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The modal remains open. No cycle is created.\n1555-\n1556-#### Test: Create cycle validates that end date is after start date\n1557:- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open.\n1558-- **Action**: User enters \"Sprint 5\" in Name, selects Feb 25 as Start date, selects Feb 12 as End date (before start), and clicks \"Create\".\n1559-- **Expected**: A validation error message appears (e.g., \"End date must be after start date\"). The modal remains open. No cycle is created.\n1560-\n1561-#### Test: Create cycle validates start and end dates are required\n1562:- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open.\n1563-- **Action**: User enters \"Sprint 5\" in Name but does not set start or end dates, and clicks \"Create\".\n1564-- **Expected**: Validation error messages appear for both date fields (e.g., \"Start date is required\", \"End date is required\"). The modal remains open. No cycle is created.\n1565-\n1566-#### Test: Cancel button closes the create cycle modal without creating\n1567:- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open. User has entered \"Sprint 5\" in the Name field.\n1568-- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\".\n1569-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new cycle is added to the cycle list. The form data is discarded.\n1570-\n1571-#### Test: Only one cycle can be active at a time per team\n1572:- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" already has an active cycle \"Sprint 2\" (Jan 15–Jan 28). Create cycle modal is open.\n1573-- **Action**: User creates a new cycle \"Sprint 5\" with dates overlapping or within the active period.\n1574-- **Expected**: Either the system prevents setting the new cycle as active while another is active (showing an appropriate message), or the new cycle is created as inactive. Only one cycle at a time has the \"active\" highlight in the cycle list.\n1575-\n1576-#### Test: Creating a cycle persists after page refresh\n1577-- **Initial state**: User has just created \"Sprint 5\" via the create cycle modal.\n1578-- **Action**: User refreshes the page.\n1579-- **Expected**: The cycle list still shows \"Sprint 5\" with the correct name, date range, and issue count of 0. The cycle was persisted to the database.\n1580-\n1581-#### Test: Create cycle modal can be opened, cancelled, and reopened\n1582-- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n1583-- **Action**: User clicks \"New Cycle\", enters \"Sprint X\" in the Name field, clicks \"Cancel\". Then user clicks \"New Cycle\" again.\n1584-- **Expected**: The modal opens fresh with empty fields on the second open. No data from the previous attempt is retained. The modal functions correctly for creating a new cycle.\n1585-\n1586-### BurndownChart\n1587-\n1588-#### Test: Burndown chart renders as a bar chart showing issues completed per day\n1589-- **Initial state**: User views cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" (Jan 15–Jan 28). Issues were completed on various days: Jan 15 (1 issue), Jan 17 (2 issues), Jan 20 (1 issue).\n1590-- **Expected**: A bar chart is displayed with the x-axis showing dates within the cycle range (Jan 15–Jan 28) and the y-axis showing the number of issues completed. Bars appear for Jan 15 (height 1), Jan 17 (height 2), Jan 20 (height 1). Days with no completions show no bar or a zero-height bar.\n1591-\n1592-#### Test: Burndown chart shows correct date range matching the cycle\n--\n1744-#### Test: Create Project button opens the create project modal\n1745:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`, no modal is open\n1746-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Create Project\" button\n1747-- **Expected**: A modal dialog opens with the title \"Create Project\" or similar. The modal overlays the page with a backdrop. The Name field is focused.\n1748-\n1749-#### Test: Create project modal renders all required fields\n1750:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1751-- **Expected**: The modal displays the following fields: Name (text input, required), Description (text area), Status (dropdown), Lead (searchable member selector), Target date (date picker), Teams (multi-select). \"Create Project\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible at the bottom.\n1752-\n1753-#### Test: Create project modal Status dropdown shows all project statuses\n1754:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1755-- **Action**: User clicks the Status dropdown\n1756-- **Expected**: Dropdown shows options: Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled. A default status is pre-selected (e.g., \"Planned\").\n1757-\n1758-#### Test: Create project modal Lead selector is searchable\n1759:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\".\n1760-- **Action**: User clicks the Lead selector and types \"Ali\"\n1761-- **Expected**: The member list filters to show only \"Alice\". User can select \"Alice\" as the lead. The selected lead shows their avatar and name.\n1762-\n1763-#### Test: Create project modal Target date uses a date picker\n1764:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1765-- **Action**: User clicks the Target date field\n1766-- **Expected**: A date picker opens allowing the user to select a date. After selecting a date (e.g., April 15, 2026), the field displays the selected date.\n1767-\n1768-#### Test: Create project modal Teams selector allows multi-select\n1769:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. Workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\".\n1770-- **Action**: User clicks the Teams selector, checks \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n1771-- **Expected**: Both teams are selected and shown as chips/badges in the Teams field. The user can deselect a team by clicking its chip or unchecking it in the dropdown.\n1772-\n1773-#### Test: Successful project creation with all fields\n1774:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1775-- **Action**: User enters \"New Feature\" in Name, \"Build the new feature\" in Description, selects \"In Progress\" status, selects \"Alice\" as lead, picks target date \"2026-05-01\", selects teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\", clicks \"Create Project\"\n1776-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new project \"New Feature\" appears in the project list with all the specified attributes (status badge \"In Progress\", lead \"Alice\", target date, progress bar at 0%, team icons for Engineering and Design). The project is persisted to the database.\n1777-\n1778-#### Test: Successful project creation with only required fields\n1779:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1780-- **Action**: User enters \"Quick Spike\" in Name, leaves all optional fields empty/default, clicks \"Create Project\"\n1781-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The project \"Quick Spike\" appears in the project list with the default status, no lead, no target date, and no teams. The project card handles missing optional fields gracefully.\n1782-\n1783-#### Test: Create project modal validates name is required\n1784:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1785-- **Action**: User leaves the Name field empty and clicks \"Create Project\"\n1786-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown for the Name field (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The modal remains open. No project is created.\n1787-\n1788-#### Test: Cancel button closes create project modal without creating\n1789:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. User has entered \"Draft Project\" in Name.\n1790-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n1791-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project named \"Draft Project\" is created. The project list remains unchanged.\n1792-\n1793-#### Test: Create project modal can be closed by clicking backdrop\n1794:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1795-- **Action**: User clicks the backdrop/overlay area outside the modal\n1796-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project is created.\n1797-\n1798-#### Test: Create project modal can be closed with Escape key\n1799:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1800-- **Action**: User presses the Escape key\n1801-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project is created.\n1802-\n1803-#### Test: Creating a project and then opening modal again resets fields\n1804-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has just created a project via the modal\n1805-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Project\" button again to open the modal\n1806-- **Expected**: All fields are reset to their defaults (Name is empty, Description is empty, Status is default, Lead is unset, Target date is unset, Teams is unset). No data from the previous creation persists in the form.\n1807-\n1808-#### Test: Created project appears immediately in the project list\n1809-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects` with 2 existing projects\n1810-- **Action**: User creates a new project \"API v3\" via the create project modal\n1811-- **Expected**: The project list now shows 3 projects, including the newly created \"API v3\". The new project appears without requiring a page refresh.\n1812-\n1813-#### Test: Create project modal Lead selector can be used multiple times\n1814:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1815-- **Action**: User selects \"Alice\" as lead, then clicks the lead selector again and changes to \"Bob\"\n1816-- **Expected**: The lead is updated to \"Bob\". The selector works correctly on repeated use. Only one lead can be selected at a time.\n1817-\n1818-#### Test: Create project modal Teams selector can be toggled multiple times\n1819:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1820-- **Action**: User selects \"Engineering\", then also selects \"Design\", then deselects \"Engineering\"\n1821-- **Expected**: Only \"Design\" remains selected. The multi-select works correctly through multiple toggle interactions.\n1822-\n1823-## Project Detail Page (`/project:projectId`)\n1824-\n1825-**Components**: ProjectHeader, ProjectIssuesTab, ProjectOverviewTab\n1826-\n1827-### ProjectHeader\n1828-\n1829-#### Test: Project header renders all fields for an existing project\n1830-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/project/1`. Project \"Auth Rewrite\" exists with status \"In Progress\", lead \"Jane Doe\", target date 2026-04-15, and 10 issues (6 completed).\n1831-- **Expected**: The header displays the project name \"Auth Rewrite\" as an inline-editable text field. A status badge shows \"In Progress\" with appropriate styling. A progress bar shows 60% completion (6/10 issues). The target date \"Apr 15, 2026\" is displayed and inline-editable. The lead shows \"Jane Doe\" with avatar and is inline-editable.\n1832-\n1833-#### Test: Inline edit project name\n1834-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n1835-- **Action**: User clicks on the project name text, clears it, types \"Auth Rewrite v2\", and presses Enter or clicks away to confirm.\n1836-- **Expected**: The project name updates to \"Auth Rewrite v2\". The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the name change.\n1837-\n1838-#### Test: Inline edit project name — cancel edit\n1839-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n--\n2300-#### Test: Create team modal Name field is required\n2301:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. Name field is empty.\n2302-- **Action**: User fills in Identifier prefix \"QA\" and clicks \"Create Team\" without entering a Name\n2303-- **Expected**: A validation error is displayed indicating the Name field is required. The modal remains open. No team is created.\n2304-\n2305-#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix is required\n2306:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. Identifier field is empty.\n2307-- **Action**: User fills in Name \"Quality Assurance\" and clicks \"Create Team\" without entering an Identifier prefix\n2308-- **Expected**: A validation error is displayed indicating the Identifier prefix is required. The modal remains open. No team is created.\n2309-\n2310-#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix must be uppercase\n2311:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2312-- **Action**: User types \"eng\" in the Identifier prefix field\n2313-- **Expected**: The input is automatically converted to uppercase \"ENG\", or a validation error is shown indicating the prefix must be uppercase.\n2314-\n2315-#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix must be 2-5 characters\n2316:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2317-- **Action**: User enters \"A\" (1 char) in the Identifier prefix field and clicks \"Create Team\"\n2318-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the prefix must be between 2 and 5 characters. The modal remains open.\n2319-\n2320-#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix rejects more than 5 characters\n2321:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2322-- **Action**: User enters \"TOOLONG\" (7 chars) in the Identifier prefix field and clicks \"Create Team\"\n2323-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the prefix must be between 2 and 5 characters, or the input is limited to 5 characters. The modal remains open.\n2324-\n2325-#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix must be unique\n2326:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. A team with identifier prefix \"ENG\" already exists.\n2327-- **Action**: User enters Name \"Engineering 2\", Identifier prefix \"ENG\", and clicks \"Create Team\"\n2328-- **Expected**: An error message is shown indicating the identifier prefix is already in use (e.g., \"A team with prefix 'ENG' already exists\"). The modal remains open. No duplicate team is created.\n2329-\n2330-#### Test: Create team with all fields filled\n2331:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. Workspace has 2 existing teams.\n2332-- **Action**: User enters Name \"Quality Assurance\", Identifier prefix \"QA\", Description \"QA team for testing\", and clicks \"Create Team\"\n2333-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The teams page now shows the new \"Quality Assurance\" team card with prefix \"QA\", member count of 0 (or 1), and no active cycle. The team is persisted (reloading shows the team).\n2334-\n2335-#### Test: Create team with only required fields\n2336:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2337-- **Action**: User enters Name \"DevOps\", Identifier prefix \"OPS\", leaves Description empty, and clicks \"Create Team\"\n2338-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new \"DevOps\" team card appears on the teams page with prefix \"OPS\" and no description issue.\n2339-\n2340-#### Test: Cancel create team modal discards input\n2341:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. User has entered Name \"Test Team\", Identifier prefix \"TT\".\n2342-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n2343-- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new team is created. The teams list remains unchanged.\n2344-\n2345-#### Test: Close create team modal by clicking backdrop\n2346:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n2347-- **Action**: User clicks outside the modal (on the backdrop overlay)\n2348-- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating a team.\n2349-\n2350-#### Test: Create team modal form resets on reopen\n2351-- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`. User previously opened the Create Team modal, entered some data, and cancelled.\n2352-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\" button again\n2353-- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields empty/reset. No residual data from the previous attempt is present.\n2354-\n2355-#### Test: Create team modal can be used multiple times in sequence\n2356-- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`.\n2357-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\", enters Name \"Team Alpha\", prefix \"ALPH\", clicks \"Create Team\". Then clicks \"Create Team\" again, enters Name \"Team Beta\", prefix \"BETA\", clicks \"Create Team\".\n2358-- **Expected**: Both teams are created. The teams page shows both new team cards. The modal opens cleanly with empty fields the second time.\n2359-\n2360-#### Test: Create team modal submits via Enter key\n2361:- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. User has entered Name \"QA Team\" and Identifier prefix \"QA\".\n2362-- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the form\n2363-- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Create Team\". The team is created if all validations pass.\n2364-\n2365-### TeamSettings\n2366-\n2367-#### Test: Team settings page renders with editable fields\n2368-- **Initial state**: Workspace has a team \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\" and description \"Core engineering team\". User clicks the \"Engineering\" team card on `/settings/teams`.\n2369-- **Expected**: The team settings view displays: Team name field showing \"Engineering\" (inline editable), Identifier prefix field showing \"ENG\" (inline editable), Description field showing \"Core engineering team\" (inline editable), and a \"Team Members\" section listing current members. A \"Back\" or navigation link to return to the teams list is visible. A \"Delete Team\" button is also present.\n2370-\n2371-#### Test: Inline edit team name\n2372-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2373-- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, changes it from \"Engineering\" to \"Platform Engineering\", and confirms (blur or Enter)\n2374-- **Expected**: The team name updates to \"Platform Engineering\". The change is persisted (reloading the page still shows \"Platform Engineering\"). The sidebar team section also reflects the updated name.\n2375-\n2376-#### Test: Inline edit team name with empty value rejected\n2377-- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n2378-- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, clears the value, and attempts to confirm\n2379-- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the team name cannot be empty. The name reverts to \"Engineering\" or the error blocks the save.\n2380-\n2381-#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix","numLines":525}}
