n    58→339-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no issues assigned to them\n    59→340-- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No issues assigned to you yet\") instead of an empty list.\n    60→341-\n    61→342-#### Test: Status group is collapsible\n    62→343-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in \"In Progress\" status, the group is expanded\n    63→344-- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n    64→--\n    65→1043-#### Test: Newly created sub-issue appears in the list\n    66→1044:- **Initial state**: User clicked \"Add sub-issue\", the create issue modal is open with parent set to \"ENG-10\"\n    67→1045-- **Action**: User fills in title \"Write unit tests\", sets status to \"Todo\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n    68→1046-- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new sub-issue (e.g., \"ENG-13 Write unit tests\") appears in the sub-issues list with a gray circle (Todo) status icon. The sub-issue is persisted with its parent reference.\n    69→1047-\n    70→1048-#### Test: Sub-issue status icon updates when status changes\n    71→1049-- **Initial state**: Sub-issue \"ENG-12\" has status \"In Progress\" (yellow half-circle) and is displayed in the parent's sub-issues list\n    72→1050-- **Action**: User navigates to \"ENG-12\", changes its status to \"Done\", and navigates back to the parent issue\n    73→1051-- **Expected**: The sub-issue \"ENG-12\" now shows a green check-circle (Done) icon in the parent's sub-issues list.\n    74→1052-\n    75→1053-#### Test: Multiple sub-issues display in correct order\n    76→1054-- **Initial state**: Parent issue has 4 sub-issues created in order: ENG-11, ENG-12, ENG-13, ENG-14\n    77→1055-- **Expected**: All 4 sub-issues are displayed in the list in a consistent order (e.g., by creation date or identifier).\n    78→1056-\n    79→1057-### ActivityComments\n    80→1058-\n    81→1059-#### Test: Activity/Comments section renders with tab toggle\n    82→1060-- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page, scrolled to the bottom of the left panel\n    83→1061-- **Expected**: The Activity/Comments section is visible with two tab buttons: \"Activity\" and \"Comments\". One tab is active (visually highlighted). A comment input box with a \"Comment\" button is visible at the bottom.\n    84→1062-\n    85→1063-#### Test: Activity tab shows chronological history\n    86→1064-- **Initial state**: An issue has had its status changed from \"Backlog\" to \"Todo\", then assignee changed from unassigned to \"Alice\", then priority changed from \"No Priority\" to \"High\"\n    87→--\n    88→1248-#### Test: Team selector allows changing team\n    89→1249:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" pre-selected. Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist.\n    90→1250-- **Action**: User clicks the Team selector dropdown and selects \"Design\"\n    91→1251-- **Expected**: Team selector now shows \"Design\". The Cycle dropdown updates to show \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" team's cycles.\n    92→1252-\n    93→1253-#### Test: Title field is required\n    94→1254:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n    95→1255-- **Action**: User leaves the Title field empty and attempts to submit\n    96→1256-- **Expected**: A validation error appears indicating that title is required. The issue is not created.\n    97→1257-\n    98→1258-#### Test: Title field accepts text input\n    99→1259:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n   100→1260-- **Action**: User types \"Implement user authentication\" in the Title field\n   101→1261-- **Expected**: The Title field displays \"Implement user authentication\".\n   102→1262-\n   103→1263-#### Test: Description field supports markdown text entry\n   104→1264:- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n   105→1265-- **Action**: User types \"## Overview\\nThis issue covers the auth flow\" in the Descripti